<p>Web excursions brought to you in partnership with <a href="https://fabric.so/?via=brett">Fabric</a>, the best way to organize your notes, tasks, and projects in one place.</p>

<dl>
  <dt><a href="https://everlog.app/blog/everlog-3-0">Everlog 3.0</a></dt>
  <dd>
    <blockquote>
      <p>Everlog 3.0 adds Gallery, Map and Moods, three new ways to look back on your journal, plus Assistants, Handoff and a new calendar.</p>
    </blockquote>
  </dd>
  <dd>
    <p>Looks like a great journaling app, including mood tracking (a necessity for me) in the premium version.</p>
  </dd>
  <dt><a href="https://www.skeinnotes.app/lede">Lede</a></dt>
  <dd>
    <blockquote>
      <p>Lede is a free, native Markdown editor for the Mac. Double-click any .md file: the syntax disappears, diagrams and maths are drawn, and the file stays yours. No subscription, no account, no Electron.</p>
    </blockquote>
  </dd>
  <dd>
    <p>Missing a few things that I think could make it better, but it&rsquo;s great for a free app and worth checking out.</p>
  </dd>
  <dt><a href="https://iconswapper.app/">IconSwapper</a></dt>
  <dd>
    <blockquote>
      <p>Shape any app icon with artwork and shaders, then bring it to life with motion and real-time data.</p>
    </blockquote>
  </dd>
  <dd>
    <p>This is a really cool customization for the Dock. I&rsquo;ve had very few issues running it, and I love the hover animations on my icons. Previously I&rsquo;d used <a href="https://replacicon.app/">Replacicon</a>, which is also great, but this is way more customizable. $29 once, currently at an intro price of $19.</p>
  </dd>
  <dt><a href="https://getrotara.app/?ref=g7">Rotara</a></dt>
  <dd>
    <blockquote>
      <p>Finally, Mac workspaces done right. Powerful workspaces for your Mac, one flick from your cursor. Each project keeps its own windows, exactly where you left them. The Spaces and Stage Manager alternative built around your projects.</p>
    </blockquote>
  </dd>
  <dd>
    <p>Pretty cool idea.</p>
  </dd>
  <dt><a href="https://diurnal.in/?ref=launchit">Diurnal</a></dt>
  <dd>
    <blockquote>
      <p>A native Mac notepad where everything you write becomes a task. Nothing needs a date, and what you stop touching tidies itself.</p>
    </blockquote>
  </dd>
  <dd>
    <p>Kind of a Noteplan idea but simpler. Free right now and worth checking out if you&rsquo;ve given up on task managers.</p>
  </dd>
</dl>

